## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design offline-first, distributed data synchronization with real-world constraints (latency, privacy, scale) in a mobile fleet context. Emphasizes secure, conflict-aware replication without centralized bottlenecks.

## Key Concepts
- WebRTC DataChannels for direct device sync
- CRDT-based namespaces for idempotent merges
- Vector clocks for causality, tombstones for deletes
- End-to-end encryption and minimal key management
- Garbage collection strategy for tombstones and stale data

## Code Example
```javascript
// useP2PQueue.ts
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import { P2PSyncManager } from './syncManager';

export const useP2PQueue = () => {
  const [pendingOps, setPendingOps] = useState([]);
  const [isConnected, setIsConnected] = useState(false);

  useEffect(() => {
    const sync = new P2PSyncManager();
    sync.onConnectionChange(setIsConnected);
    sync.onPendingOpsChange(setPendingOps);
    return () => sync.disconnect();
  }, []);

  const enqueue = async (namespace, operation) => {
    await syncManager.enqueueOperation(namespace, operation);
  };

  return { pendingOps, isConnected, enqueue };
};
```

## Trade-offs
- **Latency**: Direct P2P reduces round-trip time vs cloud relay
- **Privacy**: Data stays on-device, no third-party exposure
- **Scalability**: Mesh topology scales linearly but requires connection management

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a responsive image loading strategy that balances UX and data usage, incorporating network state, device capabilities, and offline caching in React Native.

## Key Concepts
- Variant selection logic using NetInfo, PixelRatio, and battery saver state
- Local caching strategy (Realm/SQLite) with TTL and cache busting
- Image loading lifecycle and prefetching to minimize jank

## Code Example
```javascript
import { useEffect, useState, useCallback } from 'react'
import NetInfo from '@react-native-community/netinfo'
import { PixelRatio } from 'react-native'

function useAdaptiveImage(sizes, baseUri) {
  const [uri, setUri] = useState(sizes.medium)
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true)
  const [error, setError] = useState(null)

  const resolveVariant = useCallback((info) => {
    const bandwidth = info.type === 'wifi' ? 1000 : info.details?.speed ?? 500
    const dpr = PixelRatio.get()
    const batterySaver = info.batterySaverEnabled
    let chosen = sizes.medium
    if (!batterySaver && bandwidth > 800 && dpr >= 2) chosen = sizes.large
    else if (bandwidth < 400) chosen = sizes.thumb
    return chosen
  }, [sizes])

  useEffect(() => {
    let mounted = true
    NetInfo.fetch().then(info => {
      if (!mounted) return
      const variant = resolveVariant(info)
      setUri(variant)
      // pretend fetch/cache logic here
      setLoading(false)
    }).catch(err => {
      if (mounted) { setError(err); setLoading(false) }
    })
    return () => { mounted = false }
  }, [resolveVariant])

  const refresh = useCallback(() => {
    setLoading(true)
    NetInfo.fetch().then(info => {
      const variant = resolveVariant(info)
      setUri(variant)
      setLoading(false)
    }).catch(err => setError(err))
  }, [resolveVariant])

  return { uri, loading, error, refresh }
}
```

